{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463678",
      "title": "What is \"Vue.js\"?",
      "lectureOrder": 2,
      "videoOrder": 2,
      "sourceHash": "3b1b438239232620a91833e15f633df45a66424f071dce8315cf7f4704d12a80",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.43,
          "end": 5.63,
          "en": "So what is Vue.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.63,
          "end": 9.13,
          "en": "or just vue as it's also called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.13,
          "end": 11.62,
          "en": "Vue.js is a JavaScript framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.62,
          "end": 13.37,
          "en": "that makes building interactive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.37,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "and reactive web frontends,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 17.76,
          "en": "which are basically web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.76,
          "end": 19.01,
          "en": "that run in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.01,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "so in the end what the user sees, easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 24.35,
          "en": "This is a nice sentence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.35,
          "end": 26.69,
          "en": "and it would be a correct definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.69,
          "end": 29.59,
          "en": "but it might not be too helpful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.59,
          "end": 31.48,
          "en": "so let me make this a bit clearer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.48,
          "end": 34.1,
          "en": "and let's highlight the important parts here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.1,
          "end": 37.72,
          "en": "And of course, one important part is JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.72,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "Vue.js is for JavaScript and it uses JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 44.21,
          "en": "it's all about JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.21,
          "end": 47.33,
          "en": "because JavaScript is the programming language",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.33,
          "end": 49.61,
          "en": "which we can use in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.61,
          "end": 51.47,
          "en": "We can run it in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.47,
          "end": 54.16,
          "en": "after a page was loaded by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.16,
          "end": 58.63,
          "en": "It allows us to manipulate what the user sees on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.63,
          "end": 61.72,
          "en": "without fetching a new page from the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.72,
          "end": 65.36,
          "en": "and that allows us to provide rich user experiences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.36,
          "end": 66.73,
          "en": "and I'll come back to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.73,
          "end": 70.27,
          "en": "rich user experiences point in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.27,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "But it's not just for JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 75.8,
          "en": "indeed Vue.js is a JavaScript framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.8,
          "end": 78.18,
          "en": "now what does framework mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "A framework, not just in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 83.26,
          "en": "but in any programming language",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.26,
          "end": 85.63,
          "en": "is basically a third party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.63,
          "end": 88.01,
          "en": "which means it's code not written by you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.01,
          "end": 89.66,
          "en": "but by someone else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.66,
          "end": 92.96000000000001,
          "en": "which exposes certain utility functionalities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.96000000000001,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "certain methods, certain tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "which you don't have to write on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 101.50999999999999,
          "en": "and that's important, unlike a regular library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.50999999999999,
          "end": 103.00999999999999,
          "en": "a framework is a library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.00999999999999,
          "end": 106.68,
          "en": "that does not just give you those extra functionalities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.68,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "but which also gives you a set of rules you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "It gives you a clear guidance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "a clear approach that you should follow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 117.92,
          "en": "when it comes to building your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.92,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "it basically gives you a clear idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "and structure of how to write your application code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 127.37,
          "en": "so it's the utility functions plus the rules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.37,
          "end": 129.04,
          "en": "Now, why would we use Vue.js?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.04,
          "end": 130.98,
          "en": "We also have that in a sentence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.98,
          "end": 133.24,
          "en": "because with it we can build interactive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.24,
          "end": 136.25,
          "en": "and reactive web frontends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.25,
          "end": 138.13,
          "en": "Reactive is a pretty fancy term,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.13,
          "end": 140.45,
          "en": "but in the end what it means is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.45,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "our app should be very responsive to what the user does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 147.32999999999998,
          "en": "If a user enters something on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.32999999999998,
          "end": 149.43,
          "en": "we want to be able to react to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 153.71,
          "en": "for example, to show validation errors below a input field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.71,
          "end": 157,
          "en": "we want to be able to show overlays with warning messages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "we wanna give a user a very modern look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 163.71,
          "en": "and feel in our web application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.71,
          "end": 167.69,
          "en": "Often we try to achieve what we know from mobile apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.69,
          "end": 170.09,
          "en": "and I'll come back to that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.09,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "So we wanna provide a great user experience in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 177.43,
          "en": "and Vue.js makes it easier for us to achieve that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177.43,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "and the web frontends part is all the important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 184.24,
          "en": "This basically means that Vue.js is involved with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.24,
          "end": 186.17,
          "en": "what the user sees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 186.17,
          "end": 188.26,
          "en": "it's not a server side framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.26,
          "end": 191.61,
          "en": "we don't use it with PHP or with node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 193.225,
          "en": "well, we can use it with all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 193.225,
          "end": 195.73,
          "en": "but simply in a combination,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.73,
          "end": 200.07999999999998,
          "en": "but it doesn't help us write better PHP or node.js code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.07999999999998,
          "end": 204.11,
          "en": "because vue.js is for the browser side JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.11,
          "end": 206.9,
          "en": "With HTML, CSS and JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 206.9,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "and possibly Vue.js in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 211.6,
          "en": "we can control what the user sees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 211.6,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "and we can provide rich user interface in the web.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 217.92000000000002,
          "en": "And Vue.js is a framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.92000000000002,
          "end": 220.31,
          "en": "that helps us with building such a JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.31,
          "end": 223.64,
          "en": "driven user interface running in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.64,
          "end": 227.43,
          "en": "for our web application that might be talking to a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 229.92000000000002,
          "en": "but it's all about the browser side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 229.92000000000002,
          "end": 231.513,
          "en": "that helps us achieve that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 233.27,
          "end": 235.79,
          "en": "Now why would we use something like Vue.js?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 235.79,
          "end": 239.64,
          "en": "Why would we want this reactive web frontend?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 239.64,
          "end": 241.37,
          "en": "Well, let's take a step back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 241.37,
          "end": 244.06,
          "en": "and let's not think about web applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 244.06,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "let's think about mobile applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 247.27,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "Mobile applications are very responsive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 252.91,
          "en": "things happen instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.91,
          "end": 255.41,
          "en": "we basically have like one screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 255.41,
          "end": 256.86,
          "en": "where we add overlays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.86,
          "end": 258.28,
          "en": "where we render lists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.28,
          "end": 260.39,
          "en": "we can navigate to different screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 260.39,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "with a smooth animation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 266.27,
          "en": "it all feels like one unit you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.27,
          "end": 270.47,
          "en": "So mobile apps and also desktop apps feel very reactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 270.47,
          "end": 273.42,
          "en": "we don't have to wait for new pages to load,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 273.42,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "we don't have to wait for HTML to be downloaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 278.02,
          "en": "and rendered by the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 278.02,
          "end": 281.32,
          "en": "instead, the entire user interface is already there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 281.32,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "the entire user interface is part of the mobile app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 285.63,
          "en": "the user installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 285.63,
          "end": 288.90999999999997,
          "en": "and the only thing that might be loaded behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.90999999999997,
          "end": 290.37,
          "en": "is data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 290.37,
          "end": 292.61,
          "en": "Now in web apps, traditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 292.61,
          "end": 295.98,
          "en": "we click a link and we wait for a new page to load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.98,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "and that happens over and over again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 300.28,
          "en": "We might enter some data in a form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 300.28,
          "end": 301.41,
          "en": "we click a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 301.41,
          "end": 303.71,
          "en": "that data is submitted and as a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 303.71,
          "end": 305.84,
          "en": "we get a new HTML page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 305.84,
          "end": 308.24,
          "en": "So in a traditional web page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 308.24,
          "end": 311.163,
          "en": "we wait for responses all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 312.02,
          "end": 314.18,
          "en": "JavaScript can help us here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 314.18,
          "end": 316.46,
          "en": "JavaScript can speed this up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 316.46,
          "end": 318.58,
          "en": "and JavaScript in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 318.58,
          "end": 321.84,
          "en": "allows us to provide a more modern web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 321.84,
          "end": 324.35,
          "en": "a more modern user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 324.35,
          "end": 327.67,
          "en": "JavaScript has the huge advantage of running in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 327.67,
          "end": 329.36,
          "en": "on the loaded page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 329.36,
          "end": 332.37,
          "en": "that means we have a language running in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 332.37,
          "end": 335.48,
          "en": "which can be used to change that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 335.48,
          "end": 338.92,
          "en": "without fetching new HTML behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 338.92,
          "end": 342.26,
          "en": "Instead, we can manipulate the HTML structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 342.26,
          "end": 345.62,
          "en": "the so-called DOM, Document Object Model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 345.62,
          "end": 348.04,
          "en": "of a page with JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 348.04,
          "end": 349.79,
          "en": "And that means that in modern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 349.79,
          "end": 352.46,
          "en": "JavaScript driven web applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 352.46,
          "end": 356.29,
          "en": "we're not sending a request to get a new HTML page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 356.29,
          "end": 359.04,
          "en": "instead, we only do this once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 359.04,
          "end": 362.8,
          "en": "and thereafter, we just exchange data behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 362.8,
          "end": 365.41,
          "en": "and we use client side JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 365.41,
          "end": 367.7,
          "en": "and possibly frameworks like Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 367.7,
          "end": 370.71,
          "en": "to update what's on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 370.71,
